node_modules/
dist/
# ffmpeg and ffprobe are large and are not ours to redistribute through our
# own git history. scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.mjs pulls them, the build packs them.
vendor/
# Generated from THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md + licenses/*.txt by make-licenses.mjs.
# Committed on purpose so the packaged app always carries it, but regenerated
# rather than edited.
# build/icon.png is TRACKED, deliberately, and it used to be ignored here.
# electron-builder points win and linux at it, `npm run dist` does not run
# `npm run icon` first, and nothing else regenerates it. So a fresh checkout
# built for Windows or Linux had no icon at all and said nothing about it.
# icon.icns is tracked for the same reason on mac; this just makes the two
# platforms consistent. The iconset stays ignored because the icns contains it.
build/icon.png
build/icon.icns
build/icon.iconset/
build/icon.ico
#
# The vector is the single source of truth and the only icon artifact in git.
# `npm run icon` rebuilds all three from it, and the release workflow runs that
# per platform before packaging: mac gets the icns from iconutil, linux and
# windows get the png. Nothing here is committed that a build can produce.
.DS_Store
._*
*.log
